    "setupNotes": [
      "Factorio 2.1.24 Space Age. 19 assembling machine 2 (no modules), red belts, fast/long-handed/bulk arms. WEST inputs, one labelled entrance each: iron plates, electronic circuits, copper plates, steel plates, stone bricks, plastic bars. EAST: eight passive provider chests in one column, one product each; each stops at its own cap, set in the constant combinator beside the fast-belt chest (edit one number). Gears, cable, red circuits, yellow belts, undergrounds, splitters, inserters and AM1 are made inside. Preserve the red ring wires, the green cap wires, all arm filters, the gear clock, the fast-inserter reserve decider and the fast-inserter feed decider. Supply electricity at the marked substation.",
      "Feed each west entrance with its labelled material only; the harness feeds every entrance as a full red belt. Iron mostly goes to the rear belt behind the bottom row, which feeds three iron-gear-wheel machines and the underground-belt, assembling-machine-1 and transport-belt machines. The electric-mining-drill, splitter, inserter and fast-inserter machines take iron from the ring, which gets it through one admission arm fed by a splitter branch.",
      "Electronic circuits are a supplied input (84/min at the floors, more when one product is drawn alone); one green-circuits supplier covers this mall.",
      "Caps live in one constant combinator next to the fast-belt chest (one negative number per product). Each chest arm runs only while its product is below its cap.",
      "Fast inserters are also a bulk-inserter ingredient. The fast-inserter machine's inserter-feed arm runs while the fast-inserter chest is below its cap or the ring holds fewer than 4 fast inserters (one decider), so the bulk-inserter machine keeps getting fast inserters while that chest is full. A second decider lets the fast-inserter chest arm take only fast inserters above a ring reserve of 14.",
      "Gear arms of the six gear-hungry finals take turns in an eight-window clock (7.5 s each); yellow belts, inserters and AM1 take gears freely because their own ring limits bound them."
    ],
